Z||000045||Slammed Fiero||02-15-2001||01:06 AM||||Oh My facts are quite straight... and to prove it I talked to our competition director tonight and he is going to email me the results. I'm a member of the club and I also act as public relations director. Zolst was NOT third. I know for a fact... Marc guimont , orange 240 Z with yellow wheels beat him , My dad in a 2200lbs corvair built for CP in the states beat him , Rick potters bright yellow Rx7 comp car that runs the one lap of america with 450hp beat him , Burl Vibert in a 83 Porsche 911 SC beat him. I was running a completely stock car. I have pics of the event..with the exception of the rear sway bar the car was stock. And who brought up the finishing place anyway??? Our club's website is down right now because were rebuilding it. Burl our competition director said he will email me the official results, and I will be glad to post them to straighten all this up.<P>The car is too damm loud .. Marcs 240 Z was running 1 and a half times the HP of Zolts car and it is acceptable , My dads 400hp 911 runs an B&B triflow exhaust all hand made and it is quiter than zolts car. Noise doesn't mean fast.<P>But I will gladly clear all this up in the next few days when I post the results.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000046||Sillhouette.com||02-15-2001||07:11 AM||||Do remember the I got this whole thing on Video.  You can modify results all you want I got it on TAPE.  <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000047||CraZyRabBit||02-15-2001||07:23 AM||||I thought this thread was about Canadian owners. Slammed and Sillouette, maybe you should start a new thread, I would be interested in the outcome. <P>BTW, am I the only Quebecer here?<P>Mike.||||reg||1
Z||000048||Slammed Fiero||02-15-2001||11:58 AM||||I can modify the results?? hahahaha. I don't need to. <P>The class that zolst and dave ran in was ASP. I remember fondly that Zolst was running a set of worn comp TA R1's. Now do you really think his fiero beat the likes of Rick potters 450Hp RX7?? Rick placed THIRD at the ONE LAP OF AMERICA , My dads corvair is known all over canada and the states , 6 divisional SCCA titles in CP , CP being dubbed the heavy metal class competing with the likes of 500hp Camaros and Mustangs. FINISHED 8th at the SCCA NATIONALS. This was competing against the likes of very well known drivers such as neal sapp and ron fellow. Anyone who knows racing knows these names , Ron just won the Daytona 24 hours I believe..and yes it is the same guy. In anycase , all these cars are fully developed and drivien by the BEST in the Province. I do however remember that zolsts car was fast , but it wasn't that fast.<P>I don't care if you have it on tape , it won't prove much and I know I sure as hell don't need to lie. Yeah my car was slow ..what do you expect it was bone stock!!! I had a set of worn 50 series tires on it.  I won't say anything more until I get the results. I believe the fastest cars were down in the low 30's , marc FTD turned a high 31 , I believe the fastest fiero turned a low 33 , I was in the 35 sec range. I wasn't trying to start a war over results , that certianally wasn't my goal, and I don't remember bringing the results up. But if results will end this then fine I will get the official results. <P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
